# Backend CORS (Strapi)

## Config

- **File:** `apps/backend/config/middlewares.ts` – `strapi::cors` config.

## Allowed headers

The `headers` array in the CORS config is sent as `Access-Control-Allow-Headers`. Any **custom request header** the frontend sends to the API must be listed here, or the browser will block the request with:

`Request header field X is not allowed by Access-Control-Allow-Headers in preflight response.`

Current allowed headers include:

- `Content-Type`, `Authorization`, `Origin`, `Accept`, `Accept-Language`
- **`x-skip-global-loader`** – used by frontend product fetches to skip the global loading overlay (`apps/frontend/src/services/product/product.ts`). If you add other custom headers in frontend API calls, add them here too.

## After changing CORS

Redeploy the backend so the new config is applied; preflight (OPTIONS) and GET responses will then allow the new headers.
